</style><h2>Blinky 1.5.12</h2><ul><li><strong>The exhaustion estimate appears on every shown account.</strong> With Show the estimate on, under Settings → Usage, a weekly limit that is unused or only lightly used says it is expected to last the window, including when the service does not state that window&#x27;s length. <a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/pull/73">#73</a></li><li><strong>An estimate that should last is green, and one that may not is amber.</strong> The line under the limit uses those two colours, both held back so they stay quieter than the percentage. <a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/pull/73">#73</a></li><li><strong>The usage card opens Blinky from a window icon.</strong> The control beside Token spend in the card header is a window symbol, and clicking it opens the main window on the pane last shown. <a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/pull/73">#73</a></li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/releases/tag/v1.5.12">Release notes on GitHub</a></p>]]></description>
